  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-plugin-update-audit",
      "text": "Read-only update auditing for direct plugin dependencies in a DeepSeek Harness Profile.\n\nThe plugin adds one tool, `plugin_update_audit`. It inventories the selected Profile and checks each direct dependency according to its declared source:"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-plugin-update-audit",
      "text": "- npm dependencies are compared with the official npm Registry `latest` manifest;\n- GitHub dependencies are compared with the repository's current `HEAD` through the GitHub API;\n- local tarballs and directories are reported as manual-review items, with SHA-256 for readable files;\n- unsupported, missing, or unreachable sources are reported per plugin without aborting the whole audit."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-plugin-update-audit",
      "text": "The tool never installs, updates, removes, or rewrites a plugin. Network access is limited to `registry.npmjs.org` and `api.github.com`; use `offline: true` for local inventory only. Local dependency paths are redacted from tool output."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile <profile> add dsh-plugin-update-audit@0.1.0\n```\n\nRestart DSH Desktop after installation."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "Ask the agent to call `plugin_update_audit`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"profile\": \"dev-lab\",\n  \"offline\": false,\n  \"timeout_ms\": 10000\n\nStatuses are advisory:\n\n- `update_available`: npm has a newer stable `latest` version;\n- `upstream_changed`: GitHub `HEAD` differs from an immutable pinned commit;\n- `local_review_required`: a local or workspace source needs an explicit rebuild and review;\n- `current`, `ahead`, `offline`, `unpinned`, `not_installed`, or `unavailable`: no automatic update conclusion is made."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "Always review release notes and source changes, create a safety snapshot, update one plugin at a time, restart DSH, and run that plugin's acceptance tests."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm install\nnpm run check\nnpm test\nnpm pack --dry-run"
    },
    {
